  "query_preview": "..\nShowers are expected to remain largely isolated through Friday. \nOccasional patches of weak, scattered trade-wind showers will be \npossible, particularly in the late night hours over the coastal \nwaters. Gentle winds tonight will become gentle to moderate Wednesday \nand hold steady before possibly decreasing with the arrival of a \ntrough Friday night. Models indicate this trough will move into or \njust north of the Marianas by Friday. So the location remains \nuncertain, however, confidence is high enough to put scattered \nshowers in the forecast for Tinian and Saipan, and isolated \nthunderstorms for all islands. By Saturday night, the isolated trade-\nwind shower regime will likely return.",
